23:56:47:099 [ 2816] | INFO  | [MGPU Bridge] [MGPU][R63] DEPTH TRANSPORT f=2401 mode=1 (TRANSPORTED AND BOUND) | producer: valid=2404 invalid=0 size-rejected=0, arm held 0 frame(s) | consumer: seals seen valid=2310 invalid=0 contract mismatches=0 | region 2560x1440 fmt=41 pitch=10240 bytes=14745600 at slot offset 14746112 of 44237312. INVALID IS NOT AN ERROR: ReShade unbinds depth in menus and scene changes, and R61 established that shipping the zeros it leaves behind would hand the model a false flat plane. An invalid frame carries the colour and says so. WHAT WOULD BE AN ERROR is contract mismatches above zero, or valid staying at zero once you are in gameplay - that means the tap is not feeding us. 100.0% of sealed frames carried depth. | GPU 1: unpacked=1885 bound=1750 skipped=0, DepthInverted=1, flag disagreements=0 (the seal crossed the adapter and the slot flag did not, so any disagreement between them is real). BOUND vs SKIPPED IS THE R61 TEST: skipped counts frames where ReShade had no depth and the model was given NONE rather than the previous frame's - open a menu mid-stream and this must move.
23:56:47:099 [ 2816] | INFO  | [MGPU Bridge] [MGPU][R78] MVEC TRANSPORT f=2401 mode=3 REAL | producer: copies=1616 missing=788 size-rejected=0 lock-skipped=0, arm held 6448 frame(s) | consumer: seals seen valid=1613 invalid=697 contract mismatches=0 flag disagreements=0 | region 2560x1440 fmt=34 pitch=10240 bytes=14745600 at slot offset 29491712 of 44237312 | GPU 1: unpacked=1614 bound=1613 skipped=137, scale=(2560.000, 1440.000). 69.8% of sealed frames carried vectors. COPIES IS THE ONE TO WATCH: it counts frames where the bind hook fired and a copy was recorded. If it stays at zero the probe published a handle nobody binds, and MVec never reaches the model whatever the rest of this line says. SKIPPED IS NOT AN ERROR - it counts frames with no vectors, which is what a menu looks like, and those frames are handed NONE rather than the last frame's motion.
23:56:47:099 [ 2816] | INFO  | [MGPU Bridge] [MGPU][R87] MVEC FRAME ALIGNMENT f=2401 | evaluates=1750 | elapsed 1=1616 2=2 3=1 4=1 5=43 6=56 7=26 8+=5 | worst=9 | 92.34% at 1. A motion vector describes ONE game frame; NR reprojects by whatever it is handed. When the frame NR blends against is older than one, history lands SHORT by this factor - zero error at rest, growing with speed, and no constant MVecScale can fix it. The scale is multiplied by this per evaluate. IF THIS LINE IS FLAT AT 1 AND THE ARTEFACT IS UNCHANGED, PACING IS ELIMINATED and what remains is units or sign. P4.1's skipped-frame counter predicts about 99.5% at 1, so a materially lower figure here is a desync no counter has shown us.
