23:57:41:418 [19984] | INFO  | [MGPU Bridge] [MGPU][R101] CALIBRATOR mode=2 site=iat | slots=40 data-slots=0 modules=137 gpa-calls=307 | resolved=1 creates=1 sr-handle=known | evaluates=3509 captured=3509 | cost 862 ns/frame | eval-copies=3509 eval-skips=0. || THE GAME'S OWN TABLE: color=0x1e3d59313d0 depth=0x1e30be773c0 MVEC=0x1e3d43fa420 output=0x1e3d5593970 | MVecScale 2560.0000,1440.0000 | jitter 0.0000,-0.1667 | Reset=0 | CreateFlags=0x3 -> DepthInverted=0 MVLowRes=1 MVJittered=0 IsHDR=1 AutoExposure=0 | quality=5 | render 2560x1440 -> display 2560x1440 | dynamic 0x0..0x0 | subrect 2560x1440 at color(0,0) depth(0,0) MV(0,0) out(0,0) | have=0xfff. || HOW TO READ IT. resolved=0 with evaluates=0 means no module asked for the entry point after we installed - either the title does not use DLSS, or it resolved before the addon loaded; the barrier path is untouched either way and is still what drives. sr-handle=UNFILTERED means we were not present for CreateFeature, so the table may be from frame generation rather than super sampling - check that render/display extents look like a supersampling pair before trusting it. MVEC here is the GAME'S answer to the question every round from R70 to R100 tried to infer; if it does not equal the handle the barrier probe armed on Dragon Sword, the probe was wrong on a title we believed, and THAT is the finding. have=0 bits name the keys this producer does not populate - Streamline and the raw SDK do not set the same subset, and the difference is a fact about the route, not a bug. MVLowRes IS DEFERRED OPTION 11 ANSWERED: 1 means the game's motion vectors are at RENDER resolution, 0 means display resolution, and we have been inferring that from buffer sizes since R83. Read it together with MVecScale - a low-res field with a display-sized scale is the shape that makes reprojection look almost right.
