23:57:59:128 [ 2816] | INFO  | [MGPU Bridge] [MGPU][R78] MVEC TRANSPORT f=4801 mode=3 REAL | producer: copies=4016 missing=788 size-rejected=0 lock-skipped=0, arm held 6448 frame(s) | consumer: seals seen valid=4013 invalid=697 contract mismatches=0 flag disagreements=0 | region 2560x1440 fmt=34 pitch=10240 bytes=14745600 at slot offset 29491712 of 44237312 | GPU 1: unpacked=4014 bound=4013 skipped=137, scale=(2560.000, 1440.000). 85.2% of sealed frames carried vectors. COPIES IS THE ONE TO WATCH: it counts frames where the bind hook fired and a copy was recorded. If it stays at zero the probe published a handle nobody binds, and MVec never reaches the model whatever the rest of this line says. SKIPPED IS NOT AN ERROR - it counts frames with no vectors, which is what a menu looks like, and those frames are handed NONE rather than the last frame's motion.
23:57:59:128 [ 2816] | INFO  | [MGPU Bridge] [MGPU][R87] MVEC FRAME ALIGNMENT f=4801 | evaluates=4150 | elapsed 1=4016 2=2 3=1 4=1 5=43 6=56 7=26 8+=5 | worst=9 | 96.77% at 1. A motion vector describes ONE game frame; NR reprojects by whatever it is handed. When the frame NR blends against is older than one, history lands SHORT by this factor - zero error at rest, growing with speed, and no constant MVecScale can fix it. The scale is multiplied by this per evaluate. IF THIS LINE IS FLAT AT 1 AND THE ARTEFACT IS UNCHANGED, PACING IS ELIMINATED and what remains is units or sign. P4.1's skipped-frame counter predicts about 99.5% at 1, so a materially lower figure here is a desync no counter has shown us.
