23:58:09:800 [ 2816] | INFO  | [MGPU Bridge] [MGPU][R87] MVEC FRAME ALIGNMENT f=5101 | evaluates=4450 | elapsed 1=4316 2=2 3=1 4=1 5=43 6=56 7=26 8+=5 | worst=9 | 96.99% at 1. A motion vector describes ONE game frame; NR reprojects by whatever it is handed. When the frame NR blends against is older than one, history lands SHORT by this factor - zero error at rest, growing with speed, and no constant MVecScale can fix it. The scale is multiplied by this per evaluate. IF THIS LINE IS FLAT AT 1 AND THE ARTEFACT IS UNCHANGED, PACING IS ELIMINATED and what remains is units or sign. P4.1's skipped-frame counter predicts about 99.5% at 1, so a materially lower figure here is a desync no counter has shown us.
